{
  "name": "alloptical_and_sfg",
  "description": "All-optical AND by sum-frequency generation: two invisible infrared inputs, A (1064 nm) and B (1550 nm), are overlapped on a dichroic and sent through a chi(2) crystal. Only when both are on does the crystal emit visible red light at 1/(1/1064 + 1/1550) = 631 nm. A second dichroic picks the red off to the OUT photodiode and the residual IR is dumped.",
